        "Note": "Zr-doped LATP synthesized by Pechini sol-gel method. Zr4+ (0.72 Å) partially substitutes Ti4+ (0.60 Å) to expand lattice and facilitate Li+ migration."
      },
      "Process_Info": {
        "Process_Category": "Pechini sol-gel synthesis",
        "Process_Text": {
          "original": "A solvent mixture was prepared by combining deionized water and nitric acid (HNO₃, 70%) in a 3:1 volume ratio, into which Ti(C₄H₉O)₄ (≥97%) was added under stirring until a transparent solution was obtained. Citric acid (≥99.5%) was introduced as a chelating agent at a molar ratio of 2:1 with respect to the total metal cations. Lithium nitrate (LiNO₃, 99%) was added with a 10 mol% excess to compensate for Li loss during high-temperature calcination, followed by the addition of Al(NO₃)₃·9H₂O (≥98.0%). Zirconium oxynitrate (ZrO(NO₃)₂·xH₂O, x = 4, 99%) was dissolved in deionized water and added according to the stoichiometric ratio. The solution pH was adjusted to 5 using NH₄OH (25–30%). Subsequently, NH₄H₂PO₄ (≥99%) was added, and ethylene glycol (99.5%) was incorporated at a 1:1 M ratio with citric acid to act as a dispersant. The resulting solution was heated at 85°C for 48 h to promote solvent evaporation, leading to gel formation. The gel was pre-calcined in a muffle furnace at 250°C for 5 h to obtain the LAZTP precursor, which was then transferred to an alumina crucible and calcined at 850°C for 5 h in air in a tube furnace to yield the crystalline LAZTP powders.",
          "simplified": "Pechini sol-gel method: Ti precursor dissolved in HNO₃/H₂O with citric acid chelating agent; LiNO₃ (10% excess), Al(NO₃)₃, ZrO(NO₃)₂ added; pH adjusted to 5 with NH₄OH; NH₄H₂PO₄ and ethylene glycol added; heated at 85°C/48h for gelation; pre-calcined at 250°C/5h; final calcination at 850°C/5h in air."
        },
        "Equipment": "Muffle furnace, tube furnace",
        "Key_Params": {
          "Synthesis_Method": "Pechini sol-gel",
