      "Microstructure_Info": {
        "Microstructure_Text": {
          "original": "The powders consisted of nanometer-sized primary particles agglomerated into secondary particles with diameters below approximately 3–5 μm. Elemental mapping by EDS revealed the homogeneous distribution of P, O, Al, Ti, and doped Zr throughout the particles. High-resolution transmission electron microscopy (HRTEM) was used to further investigate the variations in lattice spacing induced by Zr doping. The interplanar distance corresponding to the (113) plane increased slightly to 0.366 nm for LAZTP-0.075, confirming lattice expansion upon Zr incorporation.",
          "simplified": "Nanometer-sized primary particles agglomerated into secondary particles (3-5 μm). Homogeneous distribution of P, O, Al, Ti, Zr confirmed by EDS. Lattice expansion confirmed by HRTEM: (113) plane spacing increased to 0.366 nm."
        },
