          "Elements_Normalized": null,
          "Measurement_Method": null
        },
        "Note": "Dual-layer structure: bottom layer with 50 wt% LAZTP in PVDF-HFP + LiTFSI (60 wt% relative to PVDF-HFP), top polymer-rich layer without oxide fillers. Total thickness: 117 μm (oxide-rich layer 69 μm, polymer-rich layer 48 μm)."
      },
      "Process_Info": {
        "Process_Category": "Solution casting",
        "Process_Text": {
          "original": "Poly(vinylidene fluoride-co-hexafluoropropylene) (PVDF-HFP, average Mw approximately ~400,000) and lithium bis(trifluoromethanesulfonyl)imide (LiTFSI, 99.95%) were dissolved in N,N-dimethylacetamide (DMAc, 99.8%) at 50°C under stirring. LiTFSI was added at 60 wt% relative to PVDF-HFP. The LAZTP powders were incorporated at 50 wt% relative to the combined weight of the polymer and oxide, and stirred for 12 h to ensure homogeneous dispersion. The slurry was cast onto a glass Petri dish and vacuum-dried at 50°C for 6 h. Subsequently, a polymer solution without oxide fillers was cast onto the top, followed by additional vacuum drying at 50°C for 24 h, forming a dual-layer membrane structure. The dried membranes were carefully peeled off at room temperature and stored in an Ar-filled glovebox.",
          "simplified": "Solution casting: PVDF-HFP + LiTFSI (60 wt% vs PVDF-HFP) dissolved in DMAc at 50°C; LAZTP added at 50 wt% (vs polymer+oxide); stirred 12h; cast and vacuum-dried at 50°C/6h; polymer solution (no oxide) cast on top; vacuum-dried at 50°C/24h."
        },
