      "Microstructure_Info": {
        "Microstructure_Text": {
          "original": "The cross-sectional SEM image of the LAZTP Dual HSE clearly reveals a distinct dual-layer structure, with the oxide-rich layer (69 μm) and the polymer-rich layer (48 μm). The dual-layer membrane exhibited smaller crystallites (~8.2 μm) and reduced porosity on the surface of the polymer-rich layer. The average crystalline domain size for LAZTP 50% HSE increased significantly to 19.1 μm. The LAZTP Dual HSE exhibited the lowest surface roughness (Ra = 0.706 μm) compared to PVDF-HFP SPE (1.21 μm) and LAZTP 50% HSE (0.947 μm).",
          "simplified": "Distinct dual-layer structure: oxide-rich layer (69 μm) + polymer-rich layer (48 μm). Smaller crystallites (~8.2 μm) on polymer-rich surface. Lowest surface roughness (Ra = 0.706 μm) among tested electrolytes."
        },
