      "Process_Info": {
        "Process_Category": "Cell assembly",
        "Process_Text": {
          "original": "LiFePO4 (LFP) cathodes were prepared by mixing LFP, Super P, and PVDF binder in an 8:1:1 ratio with N-methyl-2-pyrrolidone (NMP) using a paste mixer. The slurry was blade-cast on Al foil, dried under vacuum at 80°C overnight, and punched into 13 mm discs with an active material loading of ~2 mg cm⁻². SSLB cells were assembled as CR2032 coin cells with LFP cathode, hybrid solid electrolyte (HSE), and Li metal anode. Galvanostatic cycling tests were conducted at 55°C in the voltage range of 2.8–4.0 V vs. Li/Li⁺ at 0.1–2.0C.",
